# Harden the parser against <script> tags & "quoted" input

Built with Rust 1.98, serde & serde_yaml.

## Reference

Keep these files in mind:

- `./docs/a<b>.md`

## Guidelines

- When working in `src/**/*.rs`: Reject input containing `<` or `&` unless it is escaped
- Keep `Record<T>` generics intact in error messages

## Preferences

- Prefer: Prefer `&str` over `String` in the "hot" paths

## Ask first

- Ask before: Changing the <envelope> tag vocabulary

## Files not to modify

- `src/**/*.rs` — Every Rust source file, including "generated" ones
- `docs/a&b/**` — Ampersand in a path

## Open questions

- Input can carry a fenced code block with markup

## Done when

Well-formed XML whose text keeps A & B < C > D and 'single' and "double" quotes intact.

## Notes

A fenced block with markup in it:

```rust
fn main() {
    if a < b && c > d {
        println!("{}", "<tag attr='v'>");
    }
}
```
